{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830", "page": "12", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/52/52_ppallen_196_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "196", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/1"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_197_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "197", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/2"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_198_thumb.jpg", "page": "3", "label": "198", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/3"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_199_thumb.jpg", "page": "4", "label": "199", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/4"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_200_thumb.jpg", "page": "5", "label": "200", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/5"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_201_thumb.jpg", "page": "6", "label": "201", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/6"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_202_thumb.jpg", "page": "7", "label": "202", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/7"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_203_thumb.jpg", "page": "8", "label": "203", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/8"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_204_thumb.jpg", "page": "9", "label": "204", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/9"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_205_thumb.jpg", "page": "10", "label": "205", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/10"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_206_thumb.jpg", "page": "11", "label": "206", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/11"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_207_thumb.jpg", "page": "12", "label": "207", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/12"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_208_thumb.jpg", "page": "13", "label": "208", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/13"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_209_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "209", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/14"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_210_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "210", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/15"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_211_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "211", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/16"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD1", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to the Church in Colesville, 2 December 1830", "editorialPageNumber": "207", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/26086/26086-0012.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> for the debt, if they only could obtain your <span class=\"underscore\">body</span>. They were there with carriages. Therefore beware of the Freemasons,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16635824846273561628\"><a href=\"#16635824846273561628\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans25\"><span id=\"documenttrans25\">25</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/hyrum-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Hyrum Smith</a> belonged to <a href=\"/place/palmyra-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Palmyra</a>’s Mount Moriah Lodge No. 112. When he left for <a href=\"/place/colesville-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Colesville</a>, he owed a small debt to <a href=\"/person/alexander-mcintyre\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Alexander McIntyre</a>, the Smiths’ family doctor. <a href=\"/person/lucy-mack-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Lucy Mack Smith</a> paid the debt in corn and beans but was subsequently visited by several men seeking payment. Not believing her that the debt had already been paid, they were about to take stored corn when <a href=\"/person/william-b-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William Smith</a> arrived and forced them to leave. (Nauvoo Masonic Lodge Minute Book, 30 Dec. 1841; Lucy Mack Smith, History, 1844–1845, <a href=\"/paper-summary/lucy-mack-smith-history-1844-1845/43\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/lucy-mack-smith-history-1844-1845\" poptitle=\"Book 4\">bk. 4</a>, [3]–[4]; Lucy Mack Smith, History, 1845, <a href=\"/paperSummary/lucy-mack-smith-history-1845?p=189\" class=\"externalLink\">181–184</a>.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\">Nauvoo Masonic Lodge Minute Book. / “Record of Na[u]voo Lodge Under Dispensation,” 1842–1846. CHL. <a href=\"https://catalog.churchofjesuschrist.org/assets?id=dafc2c46-c417-41d2-a25f-fceb98ca2f09&amp;crate=0&amp;index=0\" class=\"externalLink\">MS 3436</a>.</p></div></div></div></aside> This from yours &amp;c.</div> <span class=\"floating-text\"> <div class=\"right wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"18130046957206950697\"><a href=\"#18130046957206950697\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans26\"><span id=\"documenttrans26\">26</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">For the annotated version of this letter, see <a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-from-oliver-cowdery-12-november-1830\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-from-oliver-cowdery-12-november-1830\" poptitle=\"Letter from Oliver Cowdery, 12 November\n1830\">Letter from Oliver Cowdery, 12 Nov. 1830</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12339693519301123539\"><a href=\"#12339693519301123539\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc13\" place=\"plc13\" title=\"Kirtland Township, Ohio\">Kirtland</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Kirtland Township, Ohio\"><p>Located ten miles south of Lake Erie. Settled by 1811. Organized by 1818. Latter-day Saint missionaries visited township, early Nov. 1830; many residents joined Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. Population in 1830 about 55 Latter-day Saints and...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/kirtland-township-ohio\">More Info</a></div></div></aside> Geauga Co. Ohio</div><div class=\"right wasptag\">Nov<span class=\"underscore\">r</span>. 12<span class=\"underscore\">th</span>. 1830</div> <div class=\" noindent wasptag\">Our beloved brethren</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">We arrived at this place two weeks this day, On our journey we called at the Buffalo tribe, but stayed a few hours only but left two books with them. We then traveled [p. 207]</div></span></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> for the debt, if they only could <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>obtain your <span class=\"underscore\">body</span>. They were <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>there with carriages. Therefore <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>beware of the Freemasons,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3638020711726379685\"><a href=\"#3638020711726379685\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans25\"><span id=\"documenttrans25\">25</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/hyrum-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Hyrum Smith</a> belonged to <a href=\"/place/palmyra-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Palmyra</a>’s Mount Moriah Lodge No. 112. When he left for <a href=\"/place/colesville-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Colesville</a>, he owed a small debt to <a href=\"/person/alexander-mcintyre\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Alexander McIntyre</a>, the Smiths’ family doctor. <a href=\"/person/lucy-mack-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Lucy Mack Smith</a> paid the debt in corn and beans but was subsequently visited by several men seeking payment. Not believing her that the debt had already been paid, they were about to take stored corn when <a href=\"/person/william-b-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William Smith</a> arrived and forced them to leave. (Nauvoo Masonic Lodge Minute Book, 30 Dec. 1841; Lucy Mack Smith, History, 1844–1845, <a href=\"/paper-summary/lucy-mack-smith-history-1844-1845/43\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/lucy-mack-smith-history-1844-1845\" poptitle=\"Book 4\">bk. 4</a>, [3]–[4]; Lucy Mack Smith, History, 1845, <a href=\"/paperSummary/lucy-mack-smith-history-1845?p=189\" class=\"externalLink\">181–184</a>.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\">Nauvoo Masonic Lodge Minute Book. / “Record of Na[u]voo Lodge Under Dispensation,” 1842–1846. CHL. <a href=\"https://catalog.churchofjesuschrist.org/assets?id=dafc2c46-c417-41d2-a25f-fceb98ca2f09&amp;crate=0&amp;index=0\" class=\"externalLink\">MS 3436</a>.</p></div></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>This from yours &amp;c.</div> <span class=\"floating-text\"> <div class=\"right wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"129331193148816214\"><a href=\"#129331193148816214\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans26\"><span id=\"documenttrans26\">26</span></a><di